  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to an Inclusive and Effective National Dialogue in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s objective is to contribute towards the foundational and institutional prerequisites for an effective and constructive national dialogue process in Ethiopia. The implementing partner is the Ethiopian National Dialogue Commission (ENDC) established by Parliament in 2021 under Proclamation 1265/2021. Support was requested by the Government of Ethiopia for UNDP to channel donor contributions through a basket fund. Support is towards the capacity building of ENDC as an independent, trusted and empowered institution as well as the timely roll-out of an inclusive, participatory, transparent and gender-sensitive national dialogue process. The project&apos;s interventions such as discussion platforms and sessions wil include the voices of all groups including women, youth, internally displaced people, people with disabilities and other disadvantaged groups from all regions as a key feature for a credible and inclusive process.</narrative>
  </description>
